   "profile_picture_url": "",
   "about": "I’m a collaborative professional with a background spanning web development, UX, digital communication, training, and cross-functional project work. Throughout my career, I’ve enjoyed the intersection of technology and people-focused problem solving — helping teams communicate clearly, creating accessible user experiences, and supporting others through learning and growth.\n\nMy experience includes front-end and UX development, presentation and demo creation, stakeholder collaboration, mentoring, training, and translating complex ideas into approachable solutions for both technical and non-technical audiences. I’ve worked across healthcare, insurance, marketing, and technology environments, often serving as a bridge between teams with different perspectives and goals.\n\nOne of the most meaningful parts of my professional journey has been mentoring and educational support work, including several years of volunteer tutoring with the University of Denver Bridge Project. Those experiences strengthened my passion for helping others build confidence, develop skills, and navigate important personal and professional transitions.\n\nI’m especially interested in opportunities involving:\n• UX and user-centered problem solving \n• Accessibility and inclusive design\n• Collaborative and mission-driven environments\n• Career development and peer support\n• Communication and presentation work\n• Mentorship and coaching\n• Training and educational resources\n\nI value curiosity, empathy, adaptability, and lifelong learning, and I’m motivated by work that helps people feel more confident, capable, and connected.",
